<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
    <artifactId>cometgui-parent</artifactId>
    <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>cometgui-provenance</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>
  <name>CometGUI :: Provenance</name>
  <description>Single-pass MD5 and SHA-256 hashing, the provenance event model, manifest writing and the provenance report.</description>

  <!--
    COVERAGE GATE ON, CURRENTLY INERT (phase 01 unit 3).  The specification
    gates "provenance logic" at >= 90% line and >= 85% branch.  The module holds only
    package-info classes today, which carry no LINE or BRANCH counters, so
    JaCoCo has no ratio to violate and the rule cannot fail: it is switched on
    and inert, which is not the same as passing.  The phase that fills this
    module inherits a live gate rather than having to remember to add one, and
    scripts/build.sh fails the build if real classes appear here while the
    switch is still true.
  -->
  <!--
    MUTATION GATE ON, AND NO LONGER INERT (phase 04).  R-TEST-02 names
    "checksum and provenance code" and "secret redaction" as critical pure
    logic, and pom.xml's <targetClasses> already lists org.cometgui.provenance.*
    for exactly that reason.  Until this phase the module compiled nothing but
    package-info classes, so the parent's default of `true` was correct: PIT
    runs with failWhenNoMutations at its default, and would have failed a
    module that had nothing to mutate.  The module now has real classes, so the
    switch goes on, and scripts/build.sh's drift check fails the build if
    critical-package code ever appears here with the gate off again.

    VERIFIED REACHING THE CODE, NOT ASSUMED.  PIT matches its glob against the
    fully qualified class name, so org.cometgui.provenance.* was expected to
    cover the subpackages this phase creates.  A gate that silently matches
    nothing is this project's signature defect, though, so the expectation was
    checked by counting mutations per class in target/pit-reports/mutations.xml
    once the first real class had landed: 8 mutations, every one of them in
    org.cometgui.provenance.hashing.StreamingHashService.  Before that class
    existed the module produced no PIT report at all, which is the "before"
    number the after is compared against.
  -->
  <properties>
    <cometgui.coverage.core.skip>false</cometgui.coverage.core.skip>
    <cometgui.mutation.skip>false</cometgui.mutation.skip>
  </properties>

  <!--
    Only the edges the specification's layering permits are declared here.
    Adding one is an architectural change: say so in the phase handoff, and
    expect the ArchUnit rules in cometgui-archtests to have an opinion.
  -->
  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
      <artifactId>cometgui-domain</artifactId>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>
</project>
